            "review_title": "Review at Som Tum Thai - Estella Place",
            "review_text": "Andrew D\nRouse Hill, Australia114 contributions\n1\nAppalling Service\nNov 2022 • Couples\nMy partner and I had checked out the menu for this restaurant last night 14/11/22. The menu looked great and it was very busy, always a good sign.\nUnfortunately when we got here, whilst we were seated immediately, on the smallest table and given menus, that’s the only staff contact for a very long time, because they can’t get off their personal mobile’s. \nAnother gentleman was seated and his order taken, easily 5 or more minutes before any staff member came near us to actually serve us. They came multiple times for the Asian couple next to us, ensuring they had everything they needed. \nFinally, after 20 or more minutes waiting, we finally had to staff member approaches to take our order.\nThe first thing to come out was my Green Curry Beef, no rice to eat it with. My partner then got his entrée, still no rice or entrée for me.\nWe eventually got rice and my partner’s main choice. Neither main had a lot meat. After we asked about my entrée again, the waiter came back to advise it would take 4 minutes to cook, Meaning it wasn’t ordered. They came out chewy, and not that fresh. \nThis is possibly the worst meal for our entire trip.\nRead more\nWritten November 15, 2022",
